==============================================================================================================
collatz_procgen_20260922_order_laws: procedural search for sign-specific ORDER laws of Syracuse orbits
U_b(x) = oddpart(3x+b), b = +1 (plus sheet) / -1 (minus sheet), positive odd x; stopped orbits x_0..x_T
(T = first index with x_T in C_b; C_+ = {1}; C_- = {1,5,7,17,25,37,41,55,61,91}); word k_i = v_2(3x_i+b),
K_j = k_0+...+k_(j-1); signed residues b*x mod M.  A window (i, i+l) is GROWTH if 3^l > 2^K, DECAY if 2^K > 3^l
(K = K_(i+l) - K_i); its GATE is g = B/(2^K - 3^l) where 2^K x_(i+l) = 3^l x_i + B, sign(B) = b.
==============================================================================================================

