## S4. Deviation spectrum (gate crossings on transients) with exact gates
  Direction lemma (PROVED): x_(i+l) - x_i = (B - (2^K - 3^l) x_i)/2^K and sign(B) = b.  Hence on the plus
  sheet a GROWTH window always goes up and only a DECAY window can fail (go up); on the minus sheet a DECAY
  window always goes down and only a GROWTH window can fail (go down); a failure needs 0 < x_i < gate.
  plus N=1000001: 148 distinct crossing windows; (type, l, K): count = {('U', 17, 27): 12, ('U', 29, 46): 56, ('U', 41, 65): 62, ('U', 46, 73): 18}
