## S7. The three best candidates
  (1) WINDOW SIGN LAW (plus-only).  "Every growth window grows": if 3^l > 2^(K_(i+l)-K_i) then
      x_(i+l) > x_i.  PLUS: PROVED for all n (2^K x_(i+l) - 3^l x_i = B > 0).  MINUS: false exactly at the
      gate crossings; smallest witness 165 -(12 odd steps, clock 19/12)-> 163; complete list at lag 12:
      165, 309, 549 (PROVED complete); lag 53 (clock 84/53): 12 windows, 2981 ... 44433 (to 10^7); no other
      lag <= 35 (PROVED).  Plus sheet 10^7: 0 failures.  STATUS: PROVED on plus, a restatement of the sign
      law sign(B) = b on windows; the new content is the anatomy (transient near-cycles at the growth-side
      convergents 19/12, 84/53; the minus cycles occupy 1/1, 3/2, 11/7).
  (2) STURMIAN RECORD LAW (minus-only).  "Consecutive running-max records are never g apart, and the first
      record is never at index g, for g with floor(g log2 3) - floor((g-1) log2 3) = 1 (g = 3, 5, 8, 10,
      13, 15, 17, ...)".  MINUS: PROVED for g <= 36 (all n), FINITE-EXACT for every g to 10^7.  PLUS: false;
      first plus witnesses (gap g: n) {17: 171, 29: 327, 41: 1287, 46: 2035} and (first-record index g: n) {17: 257, 29: 685, 41: 2897, 46: 3053}; every witness window is a plus
      gate crossing.  STATUS: the word part is PROVED; the sheet asymmetry is the sign law again (plus
      crossings are decay windows that go up, and only they can create an excluded first passage).
  (3) COEFFICIENT STOPPING TIME sigma(n) = tau(n) (BOTH sheets; order-based, not a word function).
      FINITE-EXACT: all 5000000 plus and 4999991 minus non-cycle odd n <= 10^7, and every orbit point.
      PROVED (computer-assisted) for tau(n) <= 38 (plus) and sigma(n) <= 35 (minus).  OPEN in general
      (Terras's coefficient stopping time conjecture on the plus sheet).  Sheet-blind as a statement;
      combined with the sign law it excludes every nontrivial positive 3n+1 cycle, while the minus cycles
      satisfy it (their words never turn decay).  It is the order law that the minus cycles do not
      violate and a plus cycle would.
